<github-data-json>
{
  "title": "Coordinators C02: Companion-repository blob IO: encrypt, put, get, verify, restore check",
  "body": "# C02: Encrypted companion-repository blob storage\n\nPart of MattFlower/limitless#953 and #902. Implements the encrypted companion-store decision (`docs/coordinators.md:103`) and C02’s immutable-object boundary (`docs/coordinators.md:346`). Checkpoint publication remains C11’s responsibility: upload and verify objects before selecting a manifest through claim CAS (`docs/coordinators.md:116`).\n\nMain already provides:\n\n- `BlobRef` and manifest encoding, hashing and parsing (`src/pipeline/portable.ts:113`, `src/pipeline/portable.ts:145`, `src/pipeline/portable.ts:151`).\n- The checkpoint seam and unchanged local default (`src/pipeline/context.ts:58`, `src/pipeline/context.ts:65`, `src/pipeline/context.ts:413`).\n- Claim-write outcomes and conditional `updateRefs` with reconciliation (`src/integrations/claim-ref.ts:17`, `src/integrations/claim-ref.ts:209`). Its parser is claim-specific (`src/integrations/claim-ref.ts:61`); retention refs must not use it.\n- The existing checkpoint pointer, `ckpt1:\u003ckey\u003e:\u003cdigest\u003e`, which carries no size (`src/integrations/claim-ref.ts:32`).\n\nAdd `src/integrations/shared-store.ts`, with no production wiring.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Authenticate before returning plaintext.** AES-256-GCM uses a separately provisioned 32-byte key and fresh random 12-byte nonce per new encryption. Associated data binds version, run, object key and role.\n2. **Immutable keys.** Within a run, a key identifies one plaintext and role. An identical repeat is idempotent; conflicting content or context never overwrites it.\n3. **Retention precedes success.** Uploading a Git blob is insufficient. `applied` requires confirmed reachability at `objects/\u003ckey\u003e` through the run’s retention ref.\n4. **Conditional, append-only retention.** Preserve the observed tree, parent the exact observed tip, and mutate refs only through GraphQL `updateRefs` with exact `beforeOid` and `force: false`.\n5. **Uncertainty blocks publication.** Only `applied` establishes retention. Storage success supplies no lease authority and does not itself commit a checkpoint.\n6. **Verify expected content.** Every read authenticates and checks SHA-256; supplied size is checked independently. Missing, inaccessible, unsupported or corrupt data blocks without fallback.\n7. **Serialize per ref.** One client mutex covers each canonical companion repository/run from fresh read through classification. Independent clients rely on GitHub CAS.\n8. **Keep private material off the wire.** Only the supplied companion token authenticates requests. Payloads are encrypted; plaintext digests, role tags and data keys do not enter remote metadata. Commit metadata is fixed and synthetic.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n### API and validation\n\n```ts\nimport type { BlobRef } from \"../pipeline/portable.ts\";\n\nexport type SharedStoreErrorCode =\n  | \"configuration\" | \"invalid\" | \"missing\" | \"corrupt\"\n  | \"unsupported\" | \"conflict\" | \"unavailable\" | \"aborted\";\n\nexport declare class SharedStoreError extends Error {\n  readonly code: SharedStoreErrorCode;\n  constructor(code: SharedStoreErrorCode);\n}\n\nexport type ExpectedBlob =\n  Pick\u003cBlobRef, \"key\" | \"digest\"\u003e & Partial\u003cPick\u003cBlobRef, \"size\"\u003e\u003e;\n\nexport type RetentionOutcome =\n  | { kind: \"applied\"; tip: string }\n  | { kind: \"unchanged\"; tip: string | null }\n  | { kind: \"moved\"; tip: string }\n  | { kind: \"unconfirmed\" };\n\nexport interface SharedStore {\n  newKey(): string;\n  put(\n    runId: string, role: string, key: string,\n    plaintext: Uint8Array, signal?: AbortSignal,\n  ): Promise\u003cRetentionOutcome & { blob: BlobRef }\u003e;\n  get(\n    runId: string, role: string, expected: ExpectedBlob,\n    signal?: AbortSignal,\n  ): Promise\u003cUint8Array\u003e;\n}\n\nexport type SharedStoreDeps = {\n  repo: string;\n  token: string;\n  dataKey: Uint8Array;\n  request?: (url: string, init: RequestInit) =\u003e Promise\u003cResponse\u003e;\n  random?: (size: number) =\u003e Uint8Array;\n  deadline?: (ms: number) =\u003e {\n    signal: AbortSignal;\n    dispose(): void;\n  };\n};\n\nexport function createSharedStore(deps: SharedStoreDeps): SharedStore;\n```\n\nConstruction validates synchronously, copies the data key and performs no IO. Canonicalize with `canonicalRepo` (`src/integrations/lease-store.ts:6`); require a nonempty token and exactly 32 key bytes. Defaults are `fetch`, cryptographic `randomBytes` and a disposable timer-backed deadline.\n\nBefore awaiting, snapshot caller-owned plaintext and descriptors. Validate run IDs against `^[0-9a-z]{6,40}$`, matching `src/pipeline/portable.ts:10`; keys as 32 hexadecimal digits; digests as 64 hexadecimal digits; optional size as a nonnegative safe integer; roles as `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$`. Normalize keys and digests to lowercase. Roles are protocol tags, never free-form text.\n\n`newKey()` encodes 16 random bytes as lowercase hexadecimal. Callers allocate keys before `put` and retain them for uncertain-attempt recovery. `put` computes and returns a complete plaintext `BlobRef` on every classified outcome. `get` accepts key and digest without size so an existing claim pointer can bootstrap a manifest read.\n\n### Envelope and transport\n\nUpload this binary frame as base64:\n\n```text\nversion: 1 byte, value 1\nnonce:   12 bytes\npayload: AES-256-GCM ciphertext\ntag:     16 bytes\n```\n\nAssociated data is UTF-8 `JSON.stringify([\"limitless-blob\", 1, runId, key, role])`. The reader supplies the role independently. Reject unknown versions, truncated frames and invalid base64; permit GitHub’s base64 line wrapping. Finish authentication before exposing bytes, then check plaintext digest and optional size. Empty plaintext is valid.\n\nEvery operation first queries authenticated repository metadata for `id`, `nameWithOwner` and `isPrivate`. Require matching canonical identity and `isPrivate === true`; use that ID for CAS. Missing or unreadable metadata blocks. Restricting the token to `\u003ccompanion-repository\u003e` is a provisioning requirement, not a permission scope C02 claims to discover.\n\nUse explicit companion-token authorization for REST and GraphQL; reject redirects and HTTP-200 GraphQL responses containing `errors`. Never call `runGh`: it delegates to repository-dependent identity selection (`src/integrations/github.ts:19`, `src/integrations/github-identity.ts:169`).\n\nEach request has a fresh **30-second deadline covering dispatch, headers and complete body consumption**. Combine it with caller cancellation, settle waits on abort, and dispose timers/listeners on every exit. Inject deadlines for deterministic tests. No automatic write retries; reconciliation below is a fresh observation with fresh request deadlines.\n\nErrors have fixed code-derived messages. Never attach response/request bodies, decrypted bytes or underlying exception text. Register the supplied credential and redact any diagnostic boundary using `src/util/proc.ts:1228` and `src/util/proc.ts:1242`.\n\n### Retention and `put`\n\nUse `refs/limitless/store/\u003crunId\u003e`. A supported tip has commit message `limitless-store: 1`, allowing one terminal newline. Its root contains only an `objects` tree; that tree contains unique normalized object keys, each mode `100644`, type `blob`. Validate response shapes and 40-digit Git OIDs. Read trees nonrecursively; reject truncated trees, unexpected entries, modes, symlinks and submodules. Pin immutable reads to observed OIDs.\n\nUnder the repository/ref mutex:\n\n1. Read the exact ref, commit and trees. Only an authenticated exact-ref HTTP 404 means absent.\n2. If the key exists, authenticate its retained blob under the supplied context and compare plaintext byte-for-byte. Matching content returns `applied` at that tip without writing; incompatible content or context throws `conflict`.\n3. Otherwise encrypt and `POST git/blobs`.\n4. Create a tree adding only `objects/\u003ckey\u003e`, using the observed root as `base_tree`; omit it for initial creation.\n5. Create a commit parented by the observed tip, or with no parents initially. Use fixed synthetic author/committer values `\u003csynthetic-name\u003e` and `\u003csynthetic-email\u003e`, never local identity. Omit dates so GitHub supplies timestamps.\n6. Check caller cancellation immediately before dispatch. Send one `updateRefs` with `beforeOid` equal to the observed tip, or forty zeroes for creation, `afterOid` equal to the new commit, and `force: false`.\n7. Validate the complete mutation response. On ambiguity, reconcile from a fresh ref read:\n\n| Observation | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| Validated successful mutation response | `applied` |\n| Fresh tip equals attempted commit | `applied` |\n| Another valid tip retains the exact attempted blob OID at the same path | `applied` |\n| Fresh tip equals old tip, or remains absent after attempted creation | `unchanged` |\n| Fresh valid tip differs and lacks the attempted mapping | `moved` |\n| Reconciliation fails, is malformed, or an existing ref disappears | `unconfirmed` |\n\nEquivalent retention requires the exact blob OID and path, never matching commit text.\n\nApply this precedence:\n\n- **Caller cancellation first:** before CAS dispatch, throw `aborted`, including cancellation during queue waits, metadata reads or uploads. After CAS dispatch and before confirmation, return `unconfirmed` and issue no further requests.\n- Otherwise, invalid inputs/configuration and validated unsupported store structure throw typed errors. Failure to establish initial remote state returns `unconfirmed`.\n- An operational failure before CAS dispatch, after establishing initial state, returns `unchanged`.\n- Any ambiguous CAS failure, including internal timeout while awaiting headers or consuming its body, triggers fresh reconciliation. Failed reconciliation returns `unconfirmed`.\n\n`unchanged` and `moved` describe observations; an outstanding request may still apply later. Neither permits checkpoint publication. Never resend a stale commit. Every explicit retry starts with a fresh read and, if the key is absent, constructs a new conditional append. Release the mutex on every exit; cancellation while queued must not later start requests.\n\n### Reads and crash recovery\n\n`get` resolves the key through the selected retention tip and fetches that Git blob. It never reads unattached uploads or substitutes local data.\n\nMissing ref, entry or blob throws `missing`; inaccessible transport or deadline expiry throws `unavailable`; malformed data, authentication failure or digest/size mismatch throws `corrupt`; unknown envelope version throws `unsupported`. Caller cancellation throws `aborted`.\n\nNo SQLite journal is needed:\n\n| Interruption | Recovery |\n| --- | --- |\n| Before retention CAS, including lost upload/tree/commit responses | No retention acknowledged; retry from fresh state. |\n| CAS applied but response lost | Same-key retry authenticates retained content and returns `applied`. |\n| Retention confirmed before claim publication | Object remains retained but unselected until C11 commits its pointer. |\n| Restart loses the attempt key | Interrupted checkpoint stays uncommitted; a new key cannot itself advance a claim. |\n\nC02 has no lease clock, expiry or retention timer. Delayed completion supplies no execution authority. C11 owns rechecking generation and lease safety after storage awaits.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdd `test/shared-store.test.ts` with injected requests, randomness and deadlines. The offline fake models immutable blobs/trees/commits, exact CAS and reachability; reject unexpected endpoints and REST ref mutations. Use deferred promises, no network, subprocesses or sleeps. Each case must fail when its protected behavior is removed.\n\n1. **Envelope and fresh nonces.** Round-trip empty and binary payloads with independently computed digest/size. Capture two newly uploaded frames; their nonce fields must equal the respective injected draws and differ. Independently decrypt both with the specified AAD.\n2. **Authentication.** Alter ciphertext, change the data key, or transplant a frame across run, key or role. Every read rejects without returning plaintext.\n3. **Claim bootstrap and independent checks.** Parse an existing-format `ckpt1:\u003ckey\u003e:\u003cdigest\u003e` pointer and read a manifest using only its key/digest plus known run/role. Separately reject wrong digest with correct size and wrong size with correct digest.\n4. **Entry-time ownership.** Defer transport, mutate the caller’s plaintext after `put`, and mutate the expected descriptor after `get`. Encryption, returned digest and validation must use the entry-time snapshots.\n5. **Validation and absence.** Reject invalid inputs before requests; reject malformed OIDs, base64, frames, trees and modes; distinguish unsupported envelope versions. Remove ref, entry and blob independently. Authorization, rate-limit and transport failures must never become absence or fallback data.\n6. **Retention before acknowledgement.** Pause before CAS: uploaded content is unreachable and `put` remains pending. After CAS it is reachable. Inspect parent, `base_tree`, path, mode, zero-OID creation and exact conditional mutation.\n7. **Immutable retry.** Same key/context/bytes returns `applied` without writes. Changed plaintext or role rejects and preserves the original mapping.\n8. **Mutex boundaries.** Same-ref puts serialize and preserve both objects; another run proceeds independently. Rejection and cancellation release the queue; an aborted queued operation sends nothing.\n9. **Independent-client races.** Race creation and appends with separate clients. One applies, one reports `moved`; explicit retry preserves the union. The test must fail with the fake’s unconditional-write mutant disabling both CAS and fast-forward enforcement.\n10. **Ambiguous outcomes and late application.** Exercise every classification row, lost responses, HTTP-200 GraphQL errors and disappearance of an existing ref. Let a CAS apply after reconciliation observed the old tip; retry must freshly read and preserve retained objects, including when the late CAS races the retry’s conditional append.\n11. **Crash boundaries.** Recreate the client after blob creation, commit creation and applied CAS before response delivery. Only retained objects are readable; same-key recovery after applied CAS is idempotent.\n12. **Cancellation precedence.** Abort during metadata read, queue wait, upload and immediately before CAS: reject `aborted`, with no ref mutation. Abort after CAS dispatch, including during response-body consumption: return `unconfirmed`, make no reconciliation requests, and recover using a new client/signal.\n13. **Full request deadlines.** Stall before headers and during body consumption, both before CAS and during CAS. Advance injected deadlines: initial-state failure is `unconfirmed`, later pre-send failure is `unchanged`, and CAS timeout starts fresh reconciliation. Confirm applied/unchanged observations and failed-reconciliation `unconfirmed`; timed-out `get` rejects `unavailable`.\n14. **Privacy and independent remote readback.** Capture headers, bodies and diagnostics: only the companion credential is used, with no plaintext payload, role, plaintext digest or key material disclosed. Reject redirects and public/mismatched metadata; secret-bearing server errors produce fixed diagnostics. Read a retained probe through a new client and separate remote requests; missing/corrupt readback rejects.\n15. **Inert construction and delayed completion.** Construction performs no requests. Round-trip with wall-clock reads throwing; commit bodies contain no dates. Deferred transport completion cannot acknowledge retention before the required response or reconciliation, and deadline handling remains active.\n\nPreserve existing portable/checkpointer coverage. Follow `test/AGENTS.md` and root verification rules; add no source-spelling or documentation tests.\n\n## Compatibility\n\n- No production caller, migration, local persisted field, config key or change to an existing API. Shared mode stays disabled; existing local runs and rollback behavior remain unchanged.\n- Existing claim pointers remain valid because manifest reads require no size. `put` still returns complete `BlobRef`s.\n- Unknown envelope versions block. Payload schema validation remains with existing portable-manifest APIs and their callers.\n- Future shared-mode rollback must drain shared work and disable admission before restoring an older release (`docs/coordinators.md:317`).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Control manifests and receipts: **C03**.\n- Run/object export, artifact authorization and holdout projection: **C09–C10**.\n- Shared checkpointer wiring, read-before-publication and claim selection: **C11**. Its integration test must pause storage, advance both clocks through unsafe suspend or replace ownership, then complete storage and assert publication is refused without refreshing the previous lease window.\n- Adoption, quarantine and stage/round replay bounds: **C13**; departure triggers and checkpoint budget: **C15**.\n- Restore-verification orchestration, enablement and rollback gates: **C24**. C02 exports no `verifyRestore`; its remote-readback test remains required.\n- Lease policy/write guards, provisioning, key rotation, garbage collection, compression, chunking and alternate backends.\n\n## Budget\n\nTarget **220 changed source lines plus tests**; **hard ceiling 250 source lines, counting every helper**, matching `docs/coordinators.md:338`.\n\nReport and split before exceeding the ceiling. If necessary, propose **C02a** for transport/envelope primitives and dependent **C02b** for retained immutable writes and reconciliation. Both remain inert until complete. Do not cut retention confirmation, authentication or ambiguous-write handling to fit.\n\n\n_Spec-reviewed 2026-10-29: no SPEC-P1; every SPEC-P2 resolved in this text._\n"
}
