  "line": 243,
  "title": "get: cancellation must win over validation once the body is read",
  "detail": "The slice matches #953 closely: 248 source lines, all 15 numbered test groups present and mutation-sensitive, authenticated decryption before any plaintext, fixed diagnostics, no retries on writes. One spec gap.\n\n`get` checks cancellation only after envelope authentication and digest/size validation (src/integrations/shared-store.ts:243). If the caller aborts after the body has been fully read and the frame is damaged, `open()` throws `corrupt` (or `unsupported` for an unknown version) before `get` can return `aborted`. That violates #953's cancellation precedence and reports an interrupted read as damaged storage.\n\nFix: check the caller's signal immediately after the blob read completes, before parsing or validating the envelope, and reject `aborted`. Keep the existing order everywhere else.\n\nAdd this regression in `describe(\"cancellation and deadlines\")`. It fails today with `corrupt` and passes with the fix:\n\n```ts\n  test(\"cancellation: get abort takes precedence over validation after its complete body\", async () => {\n    const remote = new Remote();\n    const payload = bytesOf(\"cancelled read\");\n    const { blob } = await remote.client().put(runId, role, keyA, payload);\n    const sha = remote.retained(runId).get(keyA) ?? \"\";\n    const frame = Buffer.from(remote.blobs.get(sha) ?? \"\", \"base64\");\n    frame[frame.length - 1] = (frame[frame.length - 1] ?? 0) ^ 1;\n    remote.blobs.set(sha, frame.toString(\"base64\"));\n    const controller = new AbortController();\n    let readingBlob = false;\n    intercept(remote, isRead(\"git/blobs/\"), async (_call, next) => {\n      readingBlob = true;\n      return next();\n    });\n    const client = remote.client({\n      deadline: () => ({\n        signal: new AbortController().signal,\n        // Disposal marks complete body consumption, before get validates the envelope.\n        dispose: () => readingBlob && controller.abort(),\n      }),\n    });\n    await rejects(client.get(runId, role, blob, controller.signal), \"aborted\");\n  });\n\n```"
 }
]
